# Running tests

The full suite is ~30s. Never run it after every edit — scope first.

## During iteration

Run the file you changed, then its owning sub-suite:

```bash
node --experimental-test-module-mocks --test src/features/game-timer/election.test.js
node --experimental-test-module-mocks --test "src/features/game-timer/**/*.test.js"
```

Sub-suite globs: `src/features/<feature>/**`, `src/composables/**`, `src/layouts/**`,
`src/router/**`, `world-builder/**`, `scripts/*.test.mjs` (CritCrafter: `scripts/critcrafter-*.test.mjs`), `functions/bgg/*`, `functions/critcrafter/**`.

## Full suite

`npm test` only before commit/PR, or when touching shared code (`src/stores/`,
`src/features/p2p/`, `src/utils/`, `src/features/p2p/test/`). The test script enumerates
every path explicitly, so it is the only thing that catches a file you forgot.

## Expensive groups

`world-builder` is ~24s of the ~30s total. Run it as its own step, never per-edit.

## Never

- **`--test-force-exit`.** It silently drops ~450 tests across 66 files and still exits 0.
  A green run with a lower `ℹ tests` count is a failure.
- Inferring success from truncated output. Check the `ℹ tests` / `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`
  summary, and never `| tail` a run and treat empty output as passing.

## If a run stalls

A stall with no output at 0% CPU is a Firebase RTDB socket, not slowness. Waiting longer
will not help. Re-run with `required_permissions: ["full_network"]`. Unit tests are
supposed to mock Firebase via `src/features/p2p/test/offlineFirebaseMocks.js` or
`src/features/p2p/test/rtdbLifecycleHarness.js` — a new hang means a test is reaching
real `ref()`/`set()`, which should be fixed rather than worked around.
